manual.craftonica.page.0=CRAFTONICA|Lab 1||Light an LED and measure current in a DC series circuit.||Use symbols, not color alone.
manual.craftonica.page.1=MATERIALS||1 5 V DC Source|1 Electrical Button|1 220 ohm Resistor|1 LED|1 Ground|1 Multimeter
manual.craftonica.page.2=TOOL||Keep a wrench nearby to correct orientation without breaking blocks.||Each click rotates a component by 90 degrees.
manual.craftonica.page.3=CONCEPTS||The source supplies 5 V at the + terminal.||GND closes the return path.||The resistor limits current and protects the LED.
manual.craftonica.page.4=LED POLARITY||Current enters the anode +, facing the source.||It exits the cathode -, facing GND.||Reversing them turns the LED off.
manual.craftonica.page.5=PREVIEW||Hold a component and aim at the ground.||The preview shows its position and terminals before placement.
manual.craftonica.page.6=BUILD THE LINE||North||[Source] [Button]|[220 ohms] [LED]|[GND]||South||Keep every block adjacent.
manual.craftonica.page.7=ORIENT||1. Source facing south.|2. Button on the north-south axis.|3. Resistor on the same axis.
manual.craftonica.page.8=ORIENT||4. LED facing north: anode toward the source.|5. GND facing north: terminal toward the LED.
manual.craftonica.page.9=CHECK||Every terminal must touch the next component.||Correct orientation with the wrench if needed.
manual.craftonica.page.10=POWER ON||Click the button to close it.||The LED should light.||If not, check the path, terminals and polarity.
manual.craftonica.page.11=MEASURE||Sneak and use to choose the mode.||Mark probe A, then probe B on terminal faces in the same network.||Expected in the nodal model:|Source: 5.00 V|Resistance: 220.00 ohms|Current: 12.99 mA
manual.craftonica.page.12=DIAGNOSE||Open the button: zero current.||Rotate the LED twice and close the button: reversed polarity.
manual.craftonica.page.13=OVERCURRENT||Place the LED correctly again.||Replace the resistor with a wire to make an unprotected path.||The LED may burn out after 20 ticks.
manual.craftonica.page.14=COMPLETE||You applied Ohm's Law per branch:||Voltage is measured between nodes and current belongs to the selected branch.||Now diagnose other faults.
